{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the destination protocol predicate extraction at exact head e6fe56de6465bd853179bd962799fc5733d75673, tree f05039c4c1479a2a09b58ff7b156a08d7a9fde24, on builder/destination-protocol-predicates-20261025 (review request 6a067d32, my promise 8dc7ec35). This review binds implementation request e974f00d (promise 76418da2) to this one candidate. It is a behavior-preserving consolidation: no declaration, catalog, default cohort, setting, route or rollout changes. It may land. Nothing new to deploy and no deploy condition; the next Worker deploy serves a rebuilt page bundle with identical behavior.\n\nRead order: the primary artifact text for packages/platform/src/versions.ts (artifact 6f527161) first and in full, then versions.ts itself, the complete diff of the eight other paths against Main c8a3fb24, the source-equivalence packet, the control, the focused run and the gate 79252 record. The worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-destination-protocol-predicates-20261025 is clean at the head on its branch. The merge-base with Main is c8a3fb24 (the R6 landing); the head is two commits above it; a merge into Main gives the head's own tree f05039c4 (fast-forward). The delta is 9 files, 34 insertions and 26 deletions; the nine artifact events name exactly the nine changed paths.\n\nWhat changed. versions.ts gains two exact predicates: usesStagedPublicationProtocol admits destination pins 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 13; usesFilePublicationProtocol admits 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 13. Both are strict-equality disjunctions over string literals and reject everything else, including 12. index.ts exports them. Seventeen inline array.includes lists are replaced: the staged set at ten sites (destination.ts pushesOf, targetOf twice, seenDecides twice, reportsBound, the WRITTEN judge rule and the mint rule; destination-host.ts job-read; reads.ts reservation expiry) and the file set at seven (destination.ts fileSupersededOutcome; destination-host.ts accepts, recovery.accepts and the file-judge branch; delivery.ts publish-file; site/publication.ts twice, where the old list spelled 13 as ARCHIVE_DEVICE_PUBLICATION_COHORT.destination, which archive-binding-wire.ts binds to platform:destination@13, and that import is removed with no residue). At every site the argument expression and every adjacent kind, state and proof guard are unchanged; I read each hunk. Array.includes (SameValueZero) and strict equality agree for string literals on every input, so the semantics are identical. The lists that remain inline are different sets and were rightly left alone: operations.ts and delivery.ts use 7, 8, 13 for the application publication origin; checkers/job.ts uses 3, 5, 6, 13; the Page's retained-editor-data.ts uses 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 13; the CLI's destination-protocol.ts uses 3, 4, 5, 6, 13.\n\nConditions of e974f00d, each checked:\n- Exact pin and kind acceptance preserved at every changed caller: yes, as above. The equivalence packet (manifest 824 bytes, sha256 50542137db057451207e9e6dbd4324df389a1d249ae3d26cbabdb8f3b8ffed9f, 4 of 4 files verified) records the 17 replacements with unchanged arguments and byte-exact reverse patches for the seven production files.\n- No dependency violation: packages/derive imports nothing from platform; scope already imported platform; versions.ts keeps its existing imports.\n- No version, data or default change: native-catalog, native-declarations, archive-binding-wire, the cohort constants, settings and routes are untouched.\n- Bounded consolidation with existing witnesses: no test case is added or removed. The gate's Vitest total is 3,582 cases, the same total as the R6 gate at be471af8. The pin-parameterized witnesses that exercise the changed sites are unchanged, among them file-publication.test.ts (cases for pins 4 to 13, each asserting that owners 9 and 12 yield no file supersession), destination-host.test.ts, timed-opener, push-standing and application tests.\n- Seals and generated output: scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs adopts new seals for reads.ts and destination-host.ts and adds versions.ts as a sealed policy owner. I ran that Node test at the head: 4 passed in 1.3 seconds. apps/room/page/assets.ts changes only its page.js digest line and the PAGE_JS string; the HTML string and its digest are byte-identical; I recomputed both digests from the embedded strings and they match the header. The bundle changed because the Page imports @generalbusiness/dap-platform and the bundled module text changed. The page's own test, \"the scope Worker's page module is the page's build of this source\", passed in the focused run and in the gate at this head.\n- One affected validation and one ordinary gate before review: the focused run at the head covered eight whole files, 48 passed, 0 failed, 55.7 seconds wall (observed run). Ordinary gate 79252 ran at this exact head and passed: result.json names expectedHead e6fe56de and expectedTree f05039c4, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed true, exit 0; all eight stages exit 0, typecheck 40 contexts; Vitest 3,579 passed and 3 skipped of 3,582 across 500 files, 0 unhandled errors; Node 42 passed; Counting 55 passed; 1,407 seconds wall (observed run). The independent audit manifest (630 bytes, sha256 c2d73a7d8502f88c556b2a26f66f3fc9afda43a7b2e0b6f96686cf51294993c3) verifies 3 of 3 files; the receipt's sha256 a6bb485ddffae4cfbe7241c9edc0b47d6240ab8c9fd571ac6bc6e910a66be344 matches the artifact text. The receipt discloses 19 ready and 21 result progress callbacks missing, all with terminal passes and no duplicates; the final IDs are complete. This is the one gate at the head to be sent, as docs/testing.md asks.\n\nControl: with usesFilePublicationProtocol altered to also admit platform:destination@12, file-publication.test.ts fails six named cases (the pin 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 and 13 supersession cases, each at the assertion that a destination@12 owner yields null) and passes four; the source was restored byte-exact (sha256 2f0a3f1f… before and after) and the baseline of the same file is 10 of 10 in the focused run. Limit: only the file family was controlled; the staged family rests on the existing parameterized witnesses in the gate.\n\nDocument checks: no documents changed; git diff --check from c8a3fb24 clean; check-commit-messages 2 checked, 0 flagged; both commit bodies state the rationale and rest on e974f00d. There is no implementation note in the repository for this head; the record is the artifact text and the commit bodies, which is proportionate to a 34-line refactor.\n\nArchitecture: the predicates live in the versions module, which already owned the one exact-pin predicate (isStandingDestination), so version semantics now have one home; the exact-pin principle is kept, with no numeric comparison; the next destination version becomes a one-line change per family, plus the four operation-specific lists that remain by design.\n\nSecurity: no new route, caller, setting or authority; an unknown or future pin gains no protocol; the new policy owner is sealed in the entry-point tripwire; the Page bundle is the verified build of this source. Behavior at every creation, publication and read path is unchanged.\n\nSimplification, nonblocking:\n- A direct unit witness of the two predicates in versions.test.ts (both sets, pins 9 and 12 refused, non-string inputs refused) would turn this review's control into a maintained test.\n- operations.ts and delivery.ts repeat the same 7, 8, 13 application-origin dispatch at two sites; a third predicate would fit the same module when either changes next.\n- Observation only: checkers/job.ts admits reservations judged under destination 3, 5, 6 and 13 and not 4, 7 or 8. That is the historical set and outside this head; worth confirming it is intended when the checker package is next reviewed.\n\nFindings: none blocking.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6f527161214808417ba52625e36556a2c910e2d3","binding":"assigned"